.TH BASENAME 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
basename \- strip directory and suffix from a filename
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B basename
\fIPATH\fR [\fISUFFIX\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print PATH with any leading directory components removed. If SUFFIX is given and matches the end of the result (and the result isn't just SUFFIX itself), it is also removed.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 if PATH is missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
